  "notes": "Oral Health \u2014 general population (1-4y through 60+, plus 3 pregnant-women age bands), First Visit and Completed-2-Visits, each split facility/non-facility. 5 geographic rows per period (NIR + 3 provinces + Bacolod HUC). Both the Age Group (col 3) and Quarter (col 4) dimensions are stacked as rows within one 'Quarterly_1' tab \u2014 the primary sheet_map plus each extra_sheets entry uses row_filter for its age band, composed automatically with the shared period_filter_column/period_labels for the quarter (D6 mechanism, see parser.py). Percentages are ALWAYS recomputed from raw counts, never the source's own % cells: Quarterly_1's percentage columns 2-4 in the chain (Non-facility First Visit %, Facility Completed-2 %, Non-facility Completed-2 %) each divide by the PREVIOUS percentage cell instead of by population in the source \u2014 a cascading bug confirmed on every row (FLAG 2), e.g. one cached cell reads 236,957.3%. Added a Completed-2-Visits <= First-Visit DQC check per facility/non-facility per band \u2014 not present in the source at all (FLAG 6). FLAG 4 (unresolved, needs the DOH encoder): the 3 pregnant-women bands' 'Projected Population' looks like it may actually be general female population of that age range, not an estimated-pregnancies count (roughly half of the matching general age band, verified for Negros Occidental Q1) \u2014 raw counts are ingested as-is, but the % for those 3 bands specifically may not mean what its label says. Quarterly only: the workbook's own Annual_1 tab is not ingested (its column indices shift by 1 vs Quarterly_1 since it lacks a Quarter column; an annual view is derived from the quarterly data already stored)."
}